{"questions":[{"question_id":"lv0vy3rc","content":"<p>Given below are two statements :</p>\n<p>Statements I : Acidity of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.448ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 640 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-hydrogens of aldehydes and ketones is responsible for Aldol reaction.</p>\n<p>Statement II : Reaction between benzaldehyde and ethanal will NOT give Cross - Aldol product.</p>\n<p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :</p>","chapter":"aldehydes-ketones-and-carboxylic-acids","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2024-online-4th-april-morning-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2024 (Online) 4th April Morning Shift","permalink":"pgiven-below-are-two-statements-p-pstatements-i--ac-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-6gfzjt7phjjakjio","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>Given below are two statements :</p>\n<p>Statements I : Acidity of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.448ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 640 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-hydrogens of aldehydes and ketones is responsible for Aldol reaction.</p>\n<p>Statement II : Reaction between benzaldehyde and ethanal will NOT give Cross - Aldol product.</p>\n<p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are correct\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>Let's analyze the given statements in detail:</p>\n\n<p><strong>Statement I:</strong> Acidity of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.448ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 640 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-hydrogens of aldehydes and ketones is responsible for Aldol reaction.</p>\n\n<p>This statement is correct. The presence of acidic <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.448ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 640 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-hydrogens in aldehydes and ketones makes it possible for these compounds to undergo deprotonation, forming enolates. These enolates can then attack the carbonyl carbon of another aldehyde or ketone, leading to the formation of the Aldol product. Therefore, the acidity of the <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.448ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 640 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-hydrogens is crucial for the Aldol reaction.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Statement II:</strong> Reaction between benzaldehyde and ethanal will NOT give Cross-Aldol product.</p>\n\n<p>This statement is incorrect. Benzaldehyde (which lacks an <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.448ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 640 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-hydrogen) can indeed react with ethanal (which has an <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.448ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 640 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-hydrogen) in a Cross-Aldol reaction. In a Cross-Aldol reaction, one molecule (ethanal) forms an enolate and reacts with another molecule (benzaldehyde), resulting in the formation of a Cross-Aldol product.</p>\n\n<p>Based on these explanations, the most appropriate answer is:</p>\n\n<p><strong>Option B</strong></p>\n\n<p>Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect.</p>"},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>नीचे दो कथन दिए गए हैं :</p>\n<p>कथन I : ऐल्डिहाइडों एवं कीटानों के <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.448ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 640 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-हाइड्रोजनों की अम्लता ऐल्डोल अभिक्रिया के लिए जिम्मेदार है।</p>\n<p>कथन II : बैन्जैल्डिहाइड एवं ऐथेनैल की अभिक्रिया क्रॉस ऐल्डोल उत्पाद नहीं देता है।</p>\n<p>उपर्युक्त कथनों के संदर्भ में नीचे दिए गए विकल्पों में से सर्वाधिक उपयुक्त उत्तर चुनें :</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"दोनों कथन I एवं कथन II गलत हैं।\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"कथन I सही है परन्तु कथन II गलत है।"},{"identifier":"C","content":"दोनों कथन I एवं कथन II सही हैं।\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"कथन I गलत है परन्तु कथन II सही है।\n"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>आइए दिए गए कथनों का विस्तार से विश्लेषण करें:</p>\n\n<p><strong>कथन I:</strong> एल्डिहाइड और कीटोन के <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.448ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 640 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-हाइड्रोजनों की अम्लता एल्डोल अभिक्रिया के लिए उत्तरदायी है।</p>\n\n<p>यह कथन सही है। एल्डिहाइड और कीटोन में अम्लीय <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.448ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 640 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-हाइड्रोजनों की उपस्थिति के कारण इन यौगिकों का विप्रोटोनीकरण होना संभव हो जाता है, जिससे एनोलेट बनते हैं। ये एनोलेट फिर किसी अन्य एल्डिहाइड या कीटोन के कार्बोनिल कार्बन पर आक्रमण कर सकते हैं, जिससे एल्डोल उत्पाद का निर्माण होता है। इसलिए, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.448ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 640 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-हाइड्रोजनों की अम्लता एल्डोल अभिक्रिया के लिए महत्वपूर्ण है।</p>\n\n<p><strong>कथन II:</strong> बेंजैल्डिहाइड और एथेनल के बीच अभिक्रिया क्रॉस-एल्डोल उत्पाद नहीं देगी।</p>\n\n<p>यह कथन गलत है। बेंजैल्डिहाइड (जिसमें <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.448ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 640 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-हाइड्रोजन नहीं है) वास्तव में एथेनल (जिसमें <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.448ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 640 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-हाइड्रोजन है) के साथ क्रॉस-एल्डोल अभिक्रिया में प्रतिक्रिया कर सकता है। क्रॉस-एल्डोल अभिक्रिया में, एक अणु (एथेनल) एनोलेट बनाता है और दूसरे अणु (बेंजैल्डिहाइड) के साथ अभिक्रिया करता है, जिसके परिणामस्वरूप क्रॉस-एल्डोल उत्पाद का निर्माण होता है।</p>\n\n<p>इन स्पष्टीकरणों के आधार पर, सबसे उपयुक्त उत्तर है:</p>\n\n<p><strong>विकल्प B</strong></p>\n\n<p>कथन I सही है लेकिन कथन II गलत है।</p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"chemical-reactions-for-aldehydes-and-ketones","type":"mcq","year":2024,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":["assertion_reason"],"yearKey":"jee-main-2024-online-4th-april-morning-shift","active":true,"options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect\n"},{"identifier":"C","c